<!DOCTYPE topic PUBLIC "-//DITA Bootstrap//DTD DITA Bootstrap Topic//EN" "bootstrap-topic.dtd">
<topic id="cards">
  <title>Cards</title>
  <shortdesc>Bootstrap’s cards provide a flexible and extensible content container with multiple variants and
    options.</shortdesc>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <indexterm>Card</indexterm>
        <indexterm>CSS
          <indexterm><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></indexterm>
        </indexterm>
        <indexterm><xmlelement>section</xmlelement></indexterm>
      </keywords>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
  <body outputclass="language-markup">
    <section id="about">
      <title>About</title>
      <p>A <b>card</b> is a flexible and extensible content container. It includes options for headers and footers, a
        wide variety of content, contextual background colors, and powerful display options. If you’re familiar with
        Bootstrap 3, cards replace Bootstrap 4.0’s panels, wells, and thumbnails. Similar functionality to those
        components is available as modifier classes for cards.</p>
    </section>
    <section id="example">
      <title>Example</title>
      <p>Cards are built with as little markup and styles as possible, but still manage to deliver a ton of control and
        customization. Built with flexbox, they offer easy alignment and mix well with other Bootstrap components. They
        have no <xmlatt>margin</xmlatt> by default, so use
        <xref href="https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/utilities/spacing/" format="html" scope="external">spacing
          utilities</xref> as needed.</p>
      <p
      >Below is an example of a basic card with mixed content and a default width. Card widths are easily customized with Bootstrap’s various
          <xref
          href="https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/components/card/#sizing"
          format="html"
          scope="external"
        >sizing options.</xref>
      </p>
    </section>
<fig>
      <title>Example</title>
      <image href="src/card/example.png" scalefit="yes"/>
    </fig>
    <tabbed-dialog style="pills" margin="t3">
      <section>
        <title>Specialization</title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/specialization/card/example.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
      <section>
        <title><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/html/card/example.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
    </tabbed-dialog>
    <section id="titles-text-and-links">
      <title>Titles, text, and links</title>
      <p>Links are added and placed next to each other by altering the <xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt> and adding
          <codeph>card-link</codeph> to an <xmlelement>xref</xmlelement> tag.</p>
      <p>Subtitles are used by adding a <xmlelement>div</xmlelement> element.</p>
    </section>
<fig>
      <title>Titles, text, and links</title>
      <image href="src/card/titles-text-and-links.png" scalefit="yes"/>
    </fig>
    <tabbed-dialog style="pills" margin="t3">
      <section>
        <title>Specialization</title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/specialization/card/titles-text-and-links.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
      <section>
        <title><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/html/card/titles-text-and-links.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
    </tabbed-dialog>
    <section id="images">
      <title>Images</title>
      <p>The first <xmlelement>image</xmlelement> within a <xmlelement
        >card</xmlelement> places an image to the top of the card
      </p>
    </section>
<fig>
      <title>Images</title>
      <image href="src/card/images.png" scalefit="yes"/>
    </fig>
    <tabbed-dialog style="pills" margin="t3">
      <section>
        <title>Specialization</title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/specialization/card/images.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
      <section>
        <title><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/html/card/images.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
    </tabbed-dialog>
    <section id="header-and-footer">
      <title>Header and footer</title>
      <p>Add an optional header and/or footer within a card using the <xmlelement
        >card-header</xmlelement> and <xmlelement>card-footer</xmlelement> elements.
      </p>
    </section>
<fig>
      <title>Header and footer</title>
